From 6c9f7d64e32f1e40b39a4a5d7767244b9fd891d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:30:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): supervisor resume op for continuation-exhausted
 cards; refuse authority asks as assignment repairs [daveey]

A card parked by the continuation limit (continuation_exhausted triage) had no
supported release from its own recovery card: kanban_unblock is fenced for every
worker profile, and the assignment route answered with a profile swap that
validate_repair_completion then accepted on profile existence alone
(t_01a191a2b59741ef / t_01a191a46f8d85ff).

- kanban_resume_exec: typed supervisor-request op {op: resume, task_id}, run only
  by the existing non-worker executor through kanban_db.unblock_task (parent
  gating kept). Preconditions re-checked at execution: newest lifecycle event is
  the continuation_exhausted block of the run the kernel refused; no live run;
  never a human_request / needs_input / capability card; target in the
  requester's creator chain (<=3 hops) or created by it; <=2 resumes per target.
  Crash after apply is redelivered as already_applied (audit in the unblocked
  event); anything stale fails closed.
- kanban_assignment_routing: a block asking to unblock/requeue/promote/resume
  another card or reset the continuation budget raises
  execution_authority_mismatch instead of reassigning, and a legacy repair for
  such an ask cannot complete.
- unblock_task: optional event_extra merged into the unblocked event.
